FrictionFormula

The Friction Formula

The friction force experienced by an object in contact with a surface is always less than or equal to the normal force experienced by the object multiplied by the coefficient of friction between the object and surface.

F_{f} \leq \mu F_{n}

where:

F_{f} [var. scal. FrictionForce] is the magnitude of the friction force
\mu [var. scal. CoefficientOfFriction] is the coefficient of friction
F_{n} [var. scal. NormalForce] is the magnitude of the normal force

